.TH MKDIR 1
.SH NAME
mkdir, rmdir \- make or remove directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkdir
.IR dir ...
.br
.B rmdir
.IR dir ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkdir
and
.B rmdir
are commands built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
.B mkdir
makes each
.I dir
(mode 0755); its parent must exist.
.B rmdir
removes each
.IR dir ,
which must be empty. Both stop at the first one that fails.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 on the first failure (or without a name).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rm (1),
.BR chmod (1),
.BR sh (1)
